  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\nIssued at 1217 PM CST SUN NOV 8 2026\n\nA fairly pleasant day is expected this afternoon, with plenty of\nsunshine. Temperatures will drop off quickly after sunset into\nthe middle to upper 30s. A small portion of the area, generally\nnorth of Montgomery through Auburn up to Alexander City, may\nremain near 40 degrees, though local microclimate effects could\nallow temperatures to reach the 36-38 degree range. Consequently,\nan area-wide Frost Advisory has been issued. The best coverage of\nfrost will be across the north and the Black Belt in the\nsouthwest, with patchy frost plausible in any county.\n\nDry air and surface high pressure will maintain dry conditions\nthrough the first half of the workweek. By midweek, the upper-\nlevel pattern becomes more active as a southern stream trough\nlifts across the Southern Plains. Moisture pooling ahead of this\nfeature brings a low chance of rain from late Wednesday through\nThursday afternoon. A stronger upper-level trough will cross the\neastern U.S. Thursday through the weekend, pushing an associated\ncold front through the area on Thursday, followed by a\nreinforcing surge of high pressure over the weekend. Due to\nlimited moisture, a dry frontal passage is expected.\n\nTemperatures will gradually warm through the workweek, with highs\nrebounding into the low-to-mid 70s by Tuesday and Wednesday.\nThursday's cold front will bring cooler air, keeping highs in the\n50s. Lows are forecast to fall into the low-to-mid 30s over the\nupcoming weekend. The latest NBM probabilities indicate a 50-70%\nchance of freezing temperatures across northern counties next\nweekend.\n\n16",
